-- title:
--   dj is non-zero in the level-N function field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $N$ be a non-zero natural number. Inside the field of formal Laurent series $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ (Hahn series over $\mathbb{Z}$ with coefficients in $K$) consider the element [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ (the Hahn series `single (-1) 1`) times the image in $K$-coefficients of the power series $\mathrm{jNum} = E_4^3\cdot \eta^{-\text{unit}}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$ with coefficients reduced into $K$; let [`ModularCurve.jqNModC K N`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) be its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$ given by `qExpand K N`. Let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC K N`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61) be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ over $K$ generated by these two Laurent series, $F = K(j(q), j(q^N))$, and let $\langle j(q)\rangle \in F$ be the element given by $j(q)$ together with its membership in $F$ as a generator. The conclusion is that the universal derivation $D \colon F \to \Omega_{F/K}$ into the module of Kähler differentials of $F$ over $K$ does not kill this element: $D(j(q)) \neq 0$.
--
--   This records that $j$ is a separating variable for the level-$N$ modular function field over an arbitrary base field, in particular that $\Omega_{F/K}$ is non-trivial, in the purely $q$-expansion-theoretic model of that field used throughout. It is invoked when differentials on the modular curve are compared with $q$-expansion coefficients and Cartier operators, and in the bound on the rank of a Hecke torsion quotient.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_D_jqModC_ne_zero.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JqCoeff
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Differentials

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.D_jqModC_ne_zero (K : Type*) [Field K] (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] :
    KaehlerDifferential.D K (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC K N)
      ⟨ModularCurve.jqModC K, ModularCurve.jqModC_mem K N⟩ ≠ 0 := by sorry
